diff -ruN '--exclude=MANIFEST.sha256' '--exclude=.pytest_cache' '--exclude=__pycache__' '--exclude=.github' a/docs/adr/0002-kernel-data-trust-planes.md b/docs/adr/0002-kernel-data-trust-planes.md
--- a/docs/adr/0002-kernel-data-trust-planes.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/docs/adr/0002-kernel-data-trust-planes.md	2026-09-16 19:19:55.429677821 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# ADR 0002 — Kernel data and trust planes
+
+Status: Accepted
+
+The EAK kernel keeps artifact storage, evidence/provenance, approval, evaluation/certification, policy, and observability behind explicit interfaces. Domain Packs remain declarative. Provider implementations may be local or remote, but provider execution never bypasses artifact ownership or policy decisions.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Artifact bytes are referenced, not embedded in ExecutionContext.
+- Cross-tenant artifact access fails closed.
+- Evidence relations are explicit and exportable to a W3C PROV-compatible projection.
+- Human approval requires an authenticated principal/role binding.
+- Internal certification is derived from explicit engineering gates, not provider self-assertion.
+- Telemetry captures identifiers/metadata by default; content capture is not required.
diff -ruN '--exclude=MANIFEST.sha256' '--exclude=.pytest_cache' '--exclude=__pycache__' '--exclude=.github' a/docs/adr/0003-langgraph-runtime-boundary.md b/docs/adr/0003-langgraph-runtime-boundary.md
--- a/docs/adr/0003-langgraph-runtime-boundary.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/docs/adr/0003-langgraph-runtime-boundary.md	2026-09-16 19:19:55.429711300 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# ADR 0003 — LangGraph is a runtime adapter
+
+Status: Accepted
+
+EAK execution identity maps to LangGraph `thread_id`. Session and conversation identifiers do not. Runtime-native objects (`Command`, interrupts, checkpoints, snapshots) do not appear in EAK schemas. Approval nodes interrupt before side effects because resumed LangGraph nodes re-enter from their beginning.
+
+The supported adapter line for MK1 is `langgraph>=1.2.11,<1.3`. CI installs the optional dependency and executes real pause/resume conformance tests. In-memory checkpointing is test-only; a production deployment must bind a durable checkpointer.
